{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "AtrnPDXiVk", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Tom Brokaw (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763219, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "cWxbW3DzGk", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Decision 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Kerry\u2019s War Record", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (White House: David Gregory) The showdown in Texas when former Senator Max Cleland appeared at President Bush\u2019s ranch to protest ads attacking Senator John Kerry\u2019s Vietnam war record featured; scenes shown; details given of Cleland\u2019s claims that Bush was behind similar attacks on Senator John McCain and himself, and of the resignation of Bush advisor Benjamin Ginsberg after admitting that he gave advice to the group attacking Kerry; Ginsberg letter quoted. [CLELAND \u2013 says these scurrilous attacks on Kerry\u2019s credibility are false.] [From Fox News, Bush advisor Karl ROVE&#134;- says no one in the Bush campaign has coordinated with Swift Boat Veterans.]", "segment_duration": 90, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763220, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "GSzVhrxH67", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Russia / Plane Crashes", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (Moscow: Donna Friesen) The investigation into the crash of 2 passenger planes that went down almost simultaneously in Russia featured; scenes shown of the wreckage at both crash sites; details given of the possibility that the planes were brought down by terrorists and of the vow by rebels in Chechnya to disrupt upcoming elections. [\u201cFlight International\u201d magazine David LEARMONT&#134;- comments on the rarity of 2 cases of ordinary failure at the same time.] [Carnegie Moscow Center terrorism analyst Alexey MALASHENKO&#134;- comments on the Chechens\u2019 fight against Russia.] \n (Studio: Tom Brokaw; Athens: Robert Hager) The circumstantial evidence pointing to terrorism or sabotage discussed; details given about the tightening of security for Russian planes coming into the US.", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63130.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763221, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "u5s0QH0fz7", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Iraq / Al-Sadr Revolt / Al-Sistani", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced.   (Baghdad: Jennifer Eccleston) The dramatic return to Iraq of Shiite leader Grand Ayatollah Ali al-Sistani, who was in Britain for medical treatment, to call for an end to Muqtada al-Sadr\u2019s uprising in Najaf featured; scenes shown of Shiite supporters heading to Najaf to protect the shrine and of US & Iraqi soldiers patrolling the streets. [Supreme Council for Islamic Revolution in Iraq Abdul Aziz al-HAKIM&#134; {thru translator} \u2013 comments on the aim to vacate Najaf from armed elements.] [US Army 1st Lt. Michael THROCKMORTON&#134;- explains the continued assaults near the shrine.] The US assault on Sunni Muslim targets in Fallujah noted; scenes shown.", "segment_duration": 100, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63410.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763222, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "D5Tq2A23gG", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Iraq / Prisoner Abuse Scandal", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) The findings of a new report on the abuse of prisoners at Abu Ghraib prison in Iraq outlined.", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63510.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763223, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "YIMNg9S0uW", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Hollywood, Florida / Marine Van Torching", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) An incident in Hollywood, Florida, where Carlos Arredondo&#134;&#134; set fire to a Marine van and himself after learning that his son had been killed in Iraq reported; scenes shown.", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63550.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763224, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "5odMYPnZl2", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Olympic Games / Political Controversies", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced.   (Athens: Jim Maceda) Controversies over international politics at the Olympic Games in Athens, Greece, featured; details given of the anger over a political ad {shown} for President Bush claiming victories in the wars in Afghanistan & Iraq and of planned marches on the US embassy in Athens by anti-war protestors who see Secretary of State Colin Powell\u2019s visit as a provocation. [Anti-war activist Panayotis YULIS&#134;- says we shouldn\u2019t allow even the Olympics to stop us from demonstrating against the war in Iraq.] The winning of Israel\u2019s first gold medal by windsurfer Gal Fridman&#134;&#134; noted.", "segment_duration": 100, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63580.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763225, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "21Ead2GDtv", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Tom Brokaw)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63680.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763226, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-25", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763219, "segment_id": "JIXC6xGrKo", "segment_broadcast_id": "p05q90yAYi", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Plavix; One-A-Day; Ex-Lax; Sam\u2019s Club; \"Hardball.\")", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63700.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763227, "network_name": "NBC", "